{{Culture of Balisca}}

In the 21st century, many [[Regions of Balisca|Baliscan regions]] have adopted [[W:Mascot|mascot]] characters, which are usually characterized by their ''[[W:Kawaii|kawaii]]'' (cute) and unsophisticated designs, often incorporating motifs that represent local culture, history or produce. They may be created by local government or other organizations to stimulate tourism and economic development. They often appear as [[W:Costumed characters|costumed characters]] at promotional events and festivals.

